==Dutch==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|nl|de|Zigeuner}}. See the German entry for further etymological information.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˌziˈɣøː.nər/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-zigeuner.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|zi|geu|ner}}
* {{rhyme|nl|øːnər}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|m|-s|zigeunertje|f=zigeunerin}}

# {{lb|nl|sometimes|offensive}} [[Gypsy]], member of the [[Roma]]
# {{lb|nl|sometimes|offensive}} [[gypsy]], person who leads a [[nomadic]] life

====Usage notes====
Some people and organizations consider the term offensive, sometimes putting {{m|nl|woonwagenbewoner}}, {{m|nl|Roma}} and {{m|nl|Sinti}} forward as neutral alternatives.[https://vrttaal.net/taaladvies-taalkwestie/zigeuner-woonwagenbewoner] Many speakers use the word ''zigeuner'' neutrally, and the term is a common word, in both informal and formal contexts, and is also often used by newspapers and state media. The perceived political incorrectness of the term ''zigeuner'' also led to equally unsuccessful renaming efforts for {{m|nl|zigeunersaus}}. Some Romani people self-identify using the term ''zigeuner''. Compounds combing the two words are also used, i.e. {{m|nl|Roma-zigeuner}} and {{m|nl|Sinti-zigeuner}}.

